function.description:
Make several file changes in one call. Use it when a change spans more than one file and they only make sense together; use `edit` for a single change. Either the whole patch applies or none of it does.

The format is line-oriented. Context lines start with a space, removed lines with `-`, added lines with `+`:

*** Begin Patch
*** Update File: src/main.rs
@@
 fn main() {
-    println!("hi");
+    println!("hello");
 }
*** Add File: src/new.rs
+fn helper() {}
*** Delete File: src/old.rs
*** End Patch

The context in an Update has to match the file exactly and appear once. Read a file before changing it.

